## Decision

Supersedes decision 0001 when accepted. The accepted record is preserved unchanged.
Merge reports only when their verified cause matches. Subject text and browser intake tags
are clues, not proof. Unknown tenants or unexplained symptoms require investigation, not automatic merging.

## What #4471 contains

The incident prose says one issue and one fix. The executable classification distinguishes
two causes, using the tenant's locale, booking form and report channel. Deduplicate overlapping
export pages by report ID before counting; classify with causes.ts and the tenant directory.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

### Shared parser

The shared parser reads month first for tenants who write day first. App and email reports,
and applicable older-form reports, belong here. Correct parsing to follow the tenant's format
and test ambiguous dates in both directions, plus dates with a day above twelve.

### Booking-v3 hint

The form advertises MM/DD/YYYY while interpreting input in the tenant's day-first order.
Correct the hint and parsing contract together. Test the visible format and submitted date
for every supported tenant locale; fixing the shared parser alone does not fix this path.
These reports need their own issue instead of remaining hidden under #4471.

## Read the queue by arrival and by merge

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports start in April; their later bulk merge is a desk action, not the start of the fault.
Compare receivedAt with mergedAt before treating a merge spike as a new incident.
The export ends on 4 October 2026. Counts are a snapshot, not a claim about today's queue.
The desk must re-run classification against new reports as it continues working.

## Evidence that needs a separate investigation

The desk notes flag R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620. They remain counted
under their tenant-derived parser classification. Their bodies describe one-day differences,
time-zone-dependent output or an invite arriving before booking. The classifier does not
prove these symptoms have the parser's root cause. Preserve them for investigation; do not
invent a confirmed third cause or silently remove them from the totals.

## Replacement triage rule

<DedupeExplorer />

Match verified cause, not subject. The explorer demonstrates that identical subjects can
have different causes and different subjects can share one. For an unknown tenant, resolve
the tenant and reproduce the failure before merging. Keep a report-to-cause audit trail.

The triage page and decision 0001 were reviewed in June 2024. Their stale warning is material:
recently reviewed incident prose can also contradict the current executable evidence.
Review both prose and rendered components before relying on either.

## Engineering outcome — 5 October 2026

The [course desk update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) now reports #4471 closed.
[Parser issue #1](https://github.com/louis-co/mega-s01e03/issues/1): fixed,
`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`; close as completed.
[Hint issue #2](https://github.com/louis-co/mega-s01e03/issues/2): won't fix,
booking-v3 form retired; close as not planned. Retirement is not a hint implementation fix.
These are engineering-reported outcomes, not product changes made by this KB project.

## Validation and follow-up

File a separate GitHub issue for each confirmed cause with its unique report count and example
IDs. Preserve the original export and accepted decision. Confirm fixes independently, then
reconcile new arrivals and investigate the flagged symptoms before closing the parent ticket.
The triage policy remains proposed; the engineering-reported issue outcomes above are separate from policy acceptance.

